Package: heterogeneity
Title: Explore Heterogeneous Effects with Causal Forests
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Saurabh", "Khanna", email = "saurabh.khanna2701@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Explores whether the effect of an independent variable on a
    dependent variable is larger for some people than for others. One call
    fits an honest causal forest via 'grf' and reports the average effect
    (also in standard deviations for a continuous outcome), the spread of the
    forest's predictions, the characteristics it used most, and profiles of
    who has smaller and larger predictions; a second function estimates the
    effect within groups of chosen characteristics. The independent variable
    can have two values (differences) or be numeric (slopes). Missing
    characteristics use native forest handling without imputation. A 'shiny'
    app provides the same descriptive workflow for uploaded data or a General
    Social Survey example, which is downloaded with 'gssr' rather than stored.
